AGENTMESH — GETTING STARTED
===========================

Prerequisites
-------------
  - Foundry  (forge, anvil, cast)   https://getfoundry.sh
  - Node.js 18+
  - pnpm


STEP 1 — Start a local blockchain
----------------------------------
Open a terminal and leave it running:

  anvil

Anvil prints 10 funded accounts with private keys.
Copy Account #0 address and private key — you will use them below.

  Example output:
    Account #0: 0xf39Fd6e51aad88F6F4ce6aB8827279cffFb92266 (10000 ETH)
    Private Key: 0xac0974bec39a17e36ba4a6b4d238ff944bacb478cbed5efcae784d7bf4f2ff80


STEP 2 — Build the contracts
------------------------------
  cd packages/contracts
  forge build

Output ABIs land in packages/contracts/out/
The backend imports them from there — do not skip this step.


STEP 3 — Deploy MockUSDC (local only)
---------------------------------------
The contracts need a USDC token address. On anvil we deploy a mock.

  MINT_TO=<ACCOUNT_0_ADDRESS> \
  forge script script/DeployMockUSDC.s.sol \
    --rpc-url http://127.0.0.1:8545 \
    --private-key <ACCOUNT_0_PRIVATE_KEY> \
    --broadcast

Copy the printed MockUSDC address.


STEP 4 — Deploy APIRegistry + X402Facilitator
-----------------------------------------------
Use the MockUSDC address from step 3.
TREASURY_ADDRESS can be any wallet — Account #1 works fine for local testing.

  USDC_ADDRESS=<MOCK_USDC_ADDRESS> \
  TREASURY_ADDRESS=<ACCOUNT_1_ADDRESS> \
  forge script script/Deploy.s.sol \
    --rpc-url http://127.0.0.1:8545 \
    --private-key <ACCOUNT_0_PRIVATE_KEY> \
    --broadcast

Copy the printed APIRegistry and X402Facilitator addresses.


STEP 5 — Configure the backend .env
-------------------------------------
Edit apps/backend/.env:

  RPC_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8545
  GATEWAY_PRIVATE_KEY=<ACCOUNT_0_PRIVATE_KEY>
  API_REGISTRY_ADDRESS=<APIREGISTRY_ADDRESS>
  X402_FACILITATOR_ADDRESS=<X402FACILITATOR_ADDRESS>
  USDC_ADDRESS=<MOCK_USDC_ADDRESS>
  PROVIDER_ADDRESS=<ACCOUNT_0_ADDRESS>

GATEWAY_PRIVATE_KEY is used by the backend to call facilitator.settle() on-chain.
PROVIDER_ADDRESS is the wallet that receives API payments.


STEP 6 — Install backend dependencies
---------------------------------------
  cd apps/backend
  pnpm install


STEP 7 — Start the backend
----------------------------
  pnpm dev

Server starts on http://localhost:3001

  GET  /                        health check
  GET  /registry/apis           list all on-chain APIs
  GET  /registry/api/:id        get single API by ID
  GET  /registry/provider/:addr get APIs by provider
  GET  /registry/stats          total API count
  GET  /payment/nonce           get a fresh nonce + deadline
  POST /payment/verify          pre-flight signature check
  GET  /payment/balance/:addr   USDC balance
  GET  /payment/status          payment layer health
  GET  /api/v1/btc              paid endpoint (0.001 USDC)


STEP 8 — Register a sample API on-chain
-----------------------------------------
  cast send <APIREGISTRY_ADDRESS> \
    "registerAPI(string,string,uint256)" \
    "BTC Price API" \
    "http://localhost:3001/api/v1/btc" \
    1000 \
    --private-key <ACCOUNT_0_PRIVATE_KEY> \
    --rpc-url http://127.0.0.1:8545

Verify it was registered:

  curl http://localhost:3001/registry/apis


STEP 9 — Approve USDC spending (agent wallet)
-----------------------------------------------
Before an agent can pay, it must approve the facilitator to spend its USDC.
Run this once per agent wallet:

  cast send <MOCK_USDC_ADDRESS> \
    "approve(address,uint256)" \
    <X402FACILITATOR_ADDRESS> \
    1000000000000 \
    --private-key <AGENT_PRIVATE_KEY> \
    --rpc-url http://127.0.0.1:8545


STEP 10 — Make a paid API call
--------------------------------
The x402 flow requires the agent to:
  1. Get a nonce from the gateway
  2. Sign the payment message
  3. Send the signed headers with the API request

Get a nonce:
  curl http://localhost:3001/payment/nonce

Sign the payment (Node.js snippet):

  const { ethers } = require("ethers");

  const facilitatorAddress = "<X402FACILITATOR_ADDRESS>";
  const payerAddress       = "<AGENT_ADDRESS>";
  const providerAddress    = "<PROVIDER_ADDRESS>";
  const amount             = 1000n;          // 0.001 USDC
  const nonce              = "<NONCE_FROM_STEP_ABOVE>";
  const deadline           = <DEADLINE_FROM_STEP_ABOVE>;

  const encoded = ethers.solidityPacked(
    ["address", "address", "address", "uint256", "bytes32", "uint256"],
    [facilitatorAddress, payerAddress, providerAddress, amount, nonce, deadline]
  );
  const hash = ethers.keccak256(encoded);
  const wallet = new ethers.Wallet("<AGENT_PRIVATE_KEY>");
  const signature = await wallet.signMessage(ethers.getBytes(hash));

  console.log("signature:", signature);

Call the paid endpoint:

  curl http://localhost:3001/api/v1/btc \
    -H "x-payment-payer: <AGENT_ADDRESS>" \
    -H "x-payment-provider: <PROVIDER_ADDRESS>" \
    -H "x-payment-amount: 1000" \
    -H "x-payment-nonce: <NONCE>" \
    -H "x-payment-deadline: <DEADLINE>" \
    -H "x-payment-signature: <SIGNATURE>"

On success the gateway returns the BTC price and settles the USDC payment
on-chain in the background via X402Facilitator.settle().


Run contract tests
-------------------
  cd packages/contracts
  forge test -vv


Troubleshooting
---------------
  "RPC not available"
    → Make sure anvil is running (step 1)

  "Invalid signature" / "Signature does not match payer"
    → The x-payment-payer header must be the address that signed the message
    → Double-check facilitatorAddress, payerAddress, providerAddress match exactly

  "Nonce used"
    → Each nonce is single-use. Get a fresh one from GET /payment/nonce

  "Provider payment failed"
    → Agent wallet has not approved the facilitator (step 9)
    → Or agent wallet has insufficient USDC balance

  ABIs not found (import error on startup)
    → Run forge build in packages/contracts first (step 2)
